    "note": "**Soil** is the top layer of the earth where plants grow, especially when you talk about its quality (*rich soil*). **Earth** means much the same, especially in gardening (*a pot of earth*). **Dirt** is the usual American everyday word, and also means anything that makes things unclean (*dirt on your shoes*). **Ground** is the surface you stand or sit on (*sit on the ground*)."
